  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "ARABIC accepts empty text and blank cells as 0, ignores case, and rejects numeric or invalid text with #VALUE!",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 build 20527, ARABIC(text) evaluates Roman numerals case-insensitively (e.g. \"XIV\" -> 14, \"i\" -> 1), returns 0 for empty text \"\" and blank cells, and returns #VALUE! for direct numbers or non-Roman strings such as \"0\" or \"1e2\". All 2,115 full-bank ARABIC rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in Excel 16.0.20527.20088 (prefix_metadata row 6) and CalcFunc-Evidence readings/excel-20527/bank2-answers-arabic-scalar.json and bank2-answers-arabic-more.json (Excel 16.0 build 20527); 2,115/2,115 full-bank rows match.",
